{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"73c4e3226421fa9099ffa7e3becd4d8452e13a083d5791c9c10e53374d7c3fa4","digest":{"component_or_area":"config-driven rebar↔Jira mapping / outbound mutation","key_entities":["mapping_config.py","config.py","config.effective_priority_map","config.effective_create_defaults","config.local_to_jira_priority","outbound_differ.py","outbound_mutation_builders.py","outbound_mapper.py","resolve_outbound_priority","_effective_priority_map_for","_effective_create_defaults_for","adapters/jira/backend.py","adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py","OutboundMapper Protocol","map_local_to_remote","map_fields_to_remote"],"problem_keywords":["priority mapping","config-driven","create defaults","per-project","soft field drift","outbound sync","jira mapping"],"propositions":["Priority mapping is made config-driven via a str-keyed per-project overlay, mirroring the S2 status_map pattern, with unmapped priorities drifting (field omitted, warn) rather than failing sync","A new str-valued per-project create_defaults axis allows specifying default field values for required-beyond-baseline fields at create time, merged before baseline computed fields","Config resolvers _effective_priority_map_for and _effective_create_defaults_for are added to outbound_differ.py and threaded through outbound_mutation_builders.py into CREATE (both maps) and UPDATE (priority_map only) payload builders","The backend Protocol map_local_to_remote and map_fields_to_remote gain optional priority_map and create_defaults kwargs, with leaf implementations in Cloud and DataCenter adapters consuming these to emit mapped priorities and merged defaults","resolve_outbound_priority helper in outbound_mapper.py returns None on unmapped priority (recording a warning via reset_drift_warnings), causing the priority field to be omitted from the payload","Test doubles across the threading path are updated to accept priority_map and create_defaults as optional kwargs, with **kw fakes absorbing them unchanged"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787768653474694001,"uuid":"281421a6-583a-419f-b2da-50029e04671f"}